+## Map Generation (Common)
+
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6114+) **Optional XML-tunable BTS/AdvCiv standard-map generation:** AdvCiv-SAS's default map generation uses the shared [`CvMapGeneratorUtil.py`](/Assets/Python/CvMapGeneratorUtil.py) helpers and [`CvMapGenerator.cpp`](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvMapGenerator.cpp) DLL behavior inherited from base AdvCiv. New independent SAS defines let players select BTS alternatives for individual shared generation steps, including standard terrain and feature generation, fractal defaults, latitude, coastal Peaks, rivers, lakes, and bonus placement/distribution, without recompiling the DLL. The defaults continue to use AdvCiv's behavior because that remains the intended AdvCiv-SAS setting. These controls do not override separate Python mapscripts, or undo the changes that AdvCiv-SAS has made to Terrain/Feature/Bonus XML Info and other map-related GlobalDefines. A fresh map also generated successfully with the complete BTS-style shared-generator setting combination; this smoke-tests the alternate branches without claiming exact BTS map parity or balance because SAS content and mapscript behavior remain independent. See the documented map-generation block in [`GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml`](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6117+) **Fixed AdvCiv's OneArea-resource fallback:** AdvCiv's capped first distribution pass could leave fewer food and luxury resources such as Banana, Wheat, Dye and Spices than their calculated targets because its uncapped second pass could not revisit landmasses already tried. The second pass now reconsiders those landmasses when needed. This does not change XML frequencies or calculated targets: mapscripts where the first pass already succeeds are directly unchanged, while mapscripts that previously undershot can gain the missing copies up to their existing targets; exact locations and later resource placement can consequently differ. See [KI#202](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#202---fixed-base-advcivs-uncapped-second-onearea-resource-pass-could-not-revisit-landmasses-capped-during-its-first-pass).
