+- **Remove from Simple Game** some mapscripts that are deemed not essential or unbalanced; they are remain playable via the **Custom Game** menu: [Big_and_Small.py](/PrivateMaps/Big_and_Small.py), [Great_Plains.py](/PrivateMaps/Great_Plains.py), [Earth2.py](/PrivateMaps/Earth2.py), [Hemispheres.py](/PrivateMaps/Hemispheres.py), [Lakes.py](/PrivateMaps/Lakes.py) (has too few lakes), [Mixed_Continents.py](/PrivateMaps/Mixed_Continents.py), [Oasis.py](/PrivateMaps/Oasis.py), [Shuffle.py](/PrivateMaps/Shuffle.py), [Tectonics.py](/PrivateMaps/Tectonics.py).
+- **Add** or **redo** the .dds (i.e. image) in **Simple Game** for mapscripts so it is more illustrative or accurate than a dark or incorrect globe map. See [Readme.md (New .dds for mapscripts in Simple Game)](/README.md#new-dds-for-mapscripts-in-simple-game) and [CIV4WorldPickerInfos.xml](/Assets/XML/Interface/CIV4WorldPickerInfos.xml).
+- **Add** new AdvCiv-SAS original maps: [SAS_Longworld](/PrivateMaps/SAS_Longworld.py): A lightweight long-format world for AdvCiv-SAS: one connected horizontal landmass with wavy borders, inspired by Ringworld3_102_mst.py but heavily simplified, similarly also [SAS_Spiky_Avenues.py](/PrivateMaps/SAS_Spiky_Avenues.py) (Compact tactical mapscript with repeated streets: each street has facing houses (spikes), a central avenue, and bridges on left/right edges to connect streets), [SAS_Large_Facing_Islands.py](/PrivateMaps/SAS_Large_Facing_Islands.py) (Each player starts on a large island, with rivals on the east and west sides, and a rival facing north or south (when world size is large enough)), and [SAS_Parallel_Lines.py](/PrivateMaps/SAS_Parallel_Lines.py) (Parallel lines mapscript where the world is optionally (default) connected horizontally (WrapX) and vertically (WrapY). Fixed number of players per line (3 or 4), and height per player). See [Readme.md (AdvCiv-SAS original mapscripts)](/README.md#advciv-sas-original-mapscripts-eg-sas_large_facing_islands-sas_longworld-sas_parallel_lines-sas_spiky_avenues).
+- **Add** and **adapt** [BTG_Cross.py](/PrivateMaps/BTG_Cross.py) mapscript (from the Beyond the Game mod (v2.43)): remove non-AdvCiv BTG options/logic, **fix script compatibility issues**, support **max player count** and up to **world size SAS48**, **change some options** (e.g., allow Desert as Default), and expose the mapscript in both **Simple Game** and **Custom Game** lists. **Increase BTG_Cross grid dimensions** with explicit per-world-size rows (instead of all derived from Huge only): **Huge** and several smaller base sizes were **too cramped**, and direct rows make the tuning adjustable. Similarly add **other BTG maps**: [BTG_Grid.py](/PrivateMaps/BTG_Grid.py), [BTG_Lagoon.py](/PrivateMaps/BTG_Lagoon.py). See also [KI#137](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#137---fixed-btg-cross-reused-huge-grid-size-for-every-world-size-of-huge-and-below).
+- **Add and adapt** [Planet_Generator_0_68.py](/PrivateMaps/Planet_Generator_0_68.py) (from [CFC](https://forums.civfanatics.com/resources/planet-generator-0-68.1817/)): keeps its core behavior (unpredictable continent shapes with balanced continent sizes) while applying AdvCiv-SAS mapscript compatibility changes, notably **world-size percentage scaling**, **removed unneeded options** (map-size override and redundant bonuses choice), and **bug fixes** (including robust direction handling). Expose the mapscript in both **Simple Game** and **Custom Game** lists. Similarly add [Equal_Islands_V2_beta.py](/PrivateMaps/Equal_Islands_V2_beta.py) (from [CFC](https://forums.civfanatics.com/resources/equal-islands-v2-beta.19405/)), [Water.py](/PrivateMaps/Water.py) (from [CFC](https://forums.civfanatics.com/resources/water.15334/)) (actually has many lakes unlike [Lakes.py](/PrivateMaps/Lakes.py); also **adjusted city spacing** that **was too wide**).
